WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:05.730
For as long as human beings have walked upon
the Earth, and looked up to the night sky

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:12.530
at the vast, inky darkness of space, we’ve
pondered a particular question over and over

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.550
again: are we truly alone in the universe?

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:19.760
Surely, it can’t be just us, right?

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.960
The stars and planets stretch out so vastly
beyond the confines of our little blue world,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:31.350
it seems that there’s at least enough room
up there for some other forms of life to exist.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:38.000
But if they do, if there’s someone… or
something out there, would they be friend

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.750
or foe?

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.870
Would an alien race be sympathetic to the
plights of humanity?

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:48.570
Or would they perhaps view us as a hostile
threat, something to be wiped out before we

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.860
have the chance to do the same to them?

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.930
How would such a race even go about introducing
itself to us?

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.930
With a swift attack?

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:58.750
A grandiose emerging from space?

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:05.590
Or maybe they’d try something far subtler,
a subterfuge, observing us from a distance,

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:10.210
watching, learning, all while hidden in plain
sight.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:15.540
To answer these questions posed throughout
the ages, the ideas that have inspired generations

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.530
of science-fiction writers, perhaps we should
turn our gaze away from the stars.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:26.400
Let’s start our story by looking instead
at something smaller, something that might

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:32.760
be the exact opposite of the incalculable
vastness of space and all the mysteries it

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:33.760
holds.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:39.840
This story, like so many others, begins not
up there among constellations, meteors, and

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.490
gas giants, but in a small, rural town.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:48.600
A satellite miles and miles away from the
busy lifestyle of the nearest city.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:53.020
A place where everyone knows each other’s
face, and where someone…

00:01:53.020 --> 00:02:00.520
no, something, has been waiting, watching,
concealed in the one place no-one would expect.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:04.990
Now, it’s worth remembering, that when you
live in a small town, being a local celebrity

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.950
is essentially just the same as infamy.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:12.810
Saying that you’re ‘really famous in your
hometown’ can be like admitting that you’re

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.870
considered the weirdest person in your direct
vicinity.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:21.030
Sometimes, the people with that mindset wind
up strutting around their tiny township in

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:26.280
the middle of nowhere, under the impression
that they’re God’s gift to every passer-by.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:31.280
Other times, they garner odd looks and whispered
stories from anyone that spots them.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.820
Gary knew more than his fair share of these
types.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:39.690
He worked at a small, family-owned convenience
store, one of those places that everyone in

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.020
town shopped at.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:46.310
Now, as any retail worker will tell you, no
one who works in a shop ever really likes

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.360
their job.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:51.960
Ultimately, it’s usually just a way to get
paid with the promise of one day being able

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.990
to wave goodbye to the cycle of stacking shelves
and manning the cash register.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:03:01.951
And so, trapped in a small-town retail job,
usually stationed in the one spot where he

00:03:01.951 --> 00:03:07.470
had to talk to every customer that came through
the door, Gary had seen them all.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:11.550
From the ordinary and the boring, to the nasty
and unreasonable.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:16.470
But on the other side of that list were the
people who were just a little bit…

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:17.470
off.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:21.840
Those customers might look a bit shady, or
act a little bit strange, not enough to draw

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.870
everyone’s attention, but still enough to
be noticed.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.900
Almost like they felt uncomfortable in their
own skin.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:34.060
One of the more infamous customers that Gary
had encountered had garnered one hell of a

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.660
reputation with his fellow employees.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:42.900
They even had a nickname for her: ‘The Duchess’,
as those working in the shop knew her.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:48.410
She seemed mostly oblivious to other people
around her, until she needed something.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:53.029
And her way of asking for help was certainly
strange to say the least.

00:03:53.029 --> 00:03:57.110
Sometimes she might be rude, or talk without
specifying which of the store’s employees

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.330
she was talking to.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:03.129
But then there were the times when she seemed
to be trying to engage in conversation with

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:05.349
Gary or one of his co-workers.

00:04:05.349 --> 00:04:09.680
The Duchess might start out speaking with
most of her own patterns, but would seem to

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:16.180
try to copy the cadence or dialect of whoever
she happened to be talking to.She’d copy

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:23.060
accents, echo back particular phrases or even
other languages, like she was mocking them…

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.589
or trying to mimic them.

00:04:25.589 --> 00:04:29.520
Naturally, every time she appeared in the
store, Gary and the rest of the staff ran

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:34.009
a mile; or at least hid in the break room
out back until the owner of the store told

00:04:34.009 --> 00:04:36.020
them all to get back to work.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:41.580
But among the employees, caution was always
advised when approaching or providing service

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:45.370
to The Duchess, as if she could snap at a
moment’s notice.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:50.520
Whenever he saw her, Gary was reminded of
his first encounter with this particular customer.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:55.580
He had been unlucky enough to be filling shelves
when The Duchess had appeared out of nowhere.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:05:00.389
She forced a basket into his hands and instructed
Gary to follow her around the shop and fill

00:05:00.389 --> 00:05:02.370
it with items that she specified.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:07.490
Afterwards, she told him to carry her bags
of shopping outside and fill her car before

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:08.490
she left.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:13.409
It was as though someone had altered Gary’s
job description to ‘butler’ without telling

00:05:13.409 --> 00:05:14.409
him.

00:05:14.409 --> 00:05:17.479
No one fully understood why she always acted
so bizarrely.

00:05:17.479 --> 00:05:21.819
There were plenty of rumors circulating of
course, ranging from the simple explanation

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:26.499
of ‘she’s from a different generation’
to the more outlandish and wild theories.

00:05:26.499 --> 00:05:31.110
While he’d never fully believed in things
like that, Gary always joked that she was

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:35.189
so disconnected because she was actually from
another planet.

00:05:35.189 --> 00:05:39.849
Sure, an alien disguised as a human coming
to do their grocery shopping at a small-town

00:05:39.849 --> 00:05:42.240
store, sounds impossible right?

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.219
Well, maybe.

00:05:44.219 --> 00:05:48.840
Around a week since his previous encounter
with the Duchess, Gary noticed another customer

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:52.490
in the store who seemed to be acting just
as unusually.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:56.379
It was a man this time, wiry and tall, but
hunched over.

00:05:56.379 --> 00:06:01.129
When the man had first come into the store,
Gary had spotted him muttering to himself.

00:06:01.129 --> 00:06:06.200
Instantly, trapped once again behind the cash
register, he felt his heart drop, immediately

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.639
assuming the man might cause trouble.

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:13.210
As he shuffled all around the store, slinking
through the aisles, Gary could overhear him

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.039
ranting about… waffles?

00:06:16.039 --> 00:06:21.919
The wire-framed man was murmuring about waffles,
how they were a pastry eaten for breakfast

00:06:21.919 --> 00:06:25.710
with syrup, how much humans enjoyed them.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:31.990
Humans, he hadn’t said ‘us’, he had
specifically used the word humans.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:36.000
The man quickly corrected himself with the
proper word, almost as if he was teaching

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.930
himself how to speak.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:43.360
Naturally, as anyone else working retail would,
Gary assumed the man was inebriated.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:47.809
As was often the case, no matter how strange
someone in the store was acting, the staff

00:06:47.809 --> 00:06:51.969
would ultimately forget all about them by
the time their long, eight-hour shift drew

00:06:51.969 --> 00:06:55.479
to a close and they were eventually allowed
to go home.

00:06:55.479 --> 00:07:01.270
But maybe it was becoming more frequent, because
for some reason, Gary couldn’t help noticing

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:05.429
even more weird behavior from people all over
town.

00:07:05.429 --> 00:07:10.840
Sometimes it’d be somebody he knew, a neighbor,
a dog-walker, the one jogger he’d see on

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:14.430
their way back from the park as he was heading
home after work.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:20.020
One day, they’d be themselves, the next
they’d be… well, alien.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:25.039
Every time he spotted one, it seemed that
another would appear the very next day.

00:07:25.039 --> 00:07:30.849
Little did Gary know; things were only due
to get even stranger still.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:35.000
Over the next month, staff from the store
stopped showing up for their shifts.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:38.800
Gary’s manager was in pieces, trying to
call his employees to find out exactly why

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.240
they weren’t notifying him about their unscheduled
absence.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:45.509
Each one never gave a clear answer.

00:07:45.509 --> 00:07:49.610
The more of them stayed home, the longer Gary
found himself having to pick up the slack

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:50.879
and cover their shifts.

00:07:50.879 --> 00:07:55.860
At first, when it was just an extra one or
two shifts a week, he didn’t mind so much.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.339
Working more hours meant extra pay.

00:07:58.339 --> 00:08:02.539
But as more and more of his colleagues seemed
to disappear without a trace, Gary started

00:08:02.539 --> 00:08:07.759
finding himself spending more time at work
than at home, and feeling pretty unhappy about

00:08:07.759 --> 00:08:09.529
it, to say the least.

00:08:09.529 --> 00:08:15.330
After all, what good is all that extra overtime
pay if you can’t get any time to spend it?

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:19.439
Just as Gary’s exhaustion from having to
work so much was reaching its peak, taking

00:08:19.439 --> 00:08:25.020
so much of a toll that he could barely stay
awake at the checkout, that’s when she appeared

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.020
again.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.710
The Duchess looked different this time though,
and definitely not as the result of a dramatic

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.009
makeover.

00:08:31.009 --> 00:08:35.870
Immediately Gary noticed some kind of… growth
swelling out from the Duchess’ shoulder.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:40.640
He didn’t want to stare – that would be
just as rude if not worse than making a comment

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:44.840
about it – but he was certain it hadn’t
been there before.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:49.940
On this particular day, The Duchess had seemingly
also decided to be more unreasonable than

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:50.990
usual.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:55.690
Instead of just making Gary carry her groceries
out to her car again, she was insisting that

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:58.990
he bring them all the way back to her house.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:03.690
Naturally, Gary told her what any reasonable
person would, explaining calmly that he couldn’t

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:08.520
leave the store during his shift, in the interest
of putting his own safety first.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:09.930
Wrong move.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:14.550
The Duchess didn’t seem to understand the
concept, repeatedly stating that this was

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:15.550
“non-negotiable”.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:21.220
Now, when someone in Gary’s line of work
is faced with an unreasonable and unusual

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:25.080
request, the only person that can come to
their aid is their manager.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:30.130
Unfortunately, a long debate with the Duchess
was a battle that Gary’s boss just couldn’t

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.130
win.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:35.210
Eventually, after talking in circles with
the Duchess, the store owner folded, telling

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:40.810
his employee to do as she asked while he stayed
behind and watched the cash register.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:45.470
Begrudgingly, Gary picked up the Duchess’
groceries as she led him out of the store.

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:47.310
Big mistake.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:51.550
Although it wasn’t far, and Gary wasn’t
really listening, the strange customer seemed

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:57.930
to be talking about a gathering she was hosting,
with a group of local townsfolk waiting at

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:58.930
her home.

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:02.770
Sure, that sounds normal enough for some small-town
folk; when there’s a limited number of people

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:08.350
who live near you, ‘loving thy neighbor’
usually becomes your only option for socializing.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:13.160
But Gary wasn’t expecting the sight that
awaited him when he arrived at the Duchess’

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.160
house.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:19.110
Just as she had said, there was a huge group
of locals there, all of them milling around

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:25.620
idly, staring at Gary with wide, unnerving
eyes, not blinking as he carried the groceries

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:26.760
indoors.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:30.710
As if that wasn’t strange enough, almost
all of them seemed to be sporting the same

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:35.820
type of growths as the Duchess, bulging out
of their shoulders or just visible under shirt

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:36.980
collars.

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:41.900
Just like back in the store, Gary tried to
force himself not to stare, never letting

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:47.500
his eyes linger for too long on one of the
silent, staring townsfolk or their strange

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.500
protrusions.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.150
But maybe he would have been safer if he’d
stared.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:57.010
Maybe he would have noticed the group of them
huddling around him, shuffling closer while

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:58.640
his back was turned.

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:02.560
If he stared, he might have spotted the hands,
reaching out towards him.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:08.090
And he might even have seen what looked like
his co-workers, the friends he had from the

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:11.550
store all huddled at the back of the room.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:16.040
As far as his boss knew, Gary returned within
a few minutes, followed shortly by the rest

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.130
of his staff.

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:21.070
The store owner spent a few minutes angrily
berating them for not showing up to work on

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:26.260
time, not thinking to question where they’d
all been or why they all came back to the

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:27.950
store when Gary did.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:33.630
Each of his employees simply stood there,
staring at him, hanging off every word like

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:37.290
it was the first time they’d heard a human
being speak.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.680
Or like they were learning how to.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:45.271
The truth was, neither Gary nor any of his
colleagues made it back to the store that

00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:46.271
day.

00:11:46.271 --> 00:11:51.140
The… things that came back in their place
only looked like Gary and the others on the

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:52.270
outside.

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:58.380
Just like the other people in town, more and
more of them had been acting strange, speaking

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:03.070
in odd patterns and sporting strange growths
on their bodies.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:07.750
No one knows how long it took for everyone
to be replaced, some mysterious organization

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.800
swept into town a few weeks later.

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:15.380
A number of people… or the things that were
disguised as people, all disappeared soon

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:16.380
after.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:20.800
Any actual humans that were left behind didn’t
notice, forgetting how many others used to

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:24.130
live in the town, as if they had been drugged.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:28.450
With the local store closing its doors, and
fewer people around, most of them packed their

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.900
belongings and moved on, heading to live elsewhere.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:34.460
Eventually, the town fell silent.

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:38.540
If you were to pass through there today, you’d
find nothing but the remains of a community

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:41.550
that gradually changed into something… alien.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:45.140
All that’s left of the place now is a ghost
town.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:48.410
You might even call it an empty shell.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:53.170
Few people would ever really understand what
happened in that small, rural town.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:55.830
Even those who did know would never admit
to it.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:59.540
The SCP Foundation is like that, as you may
well know.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:04.550
They’re shady, secretive and would much
rather keep to themselves, not unlike that

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.200
group of townsfolk, actually.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:12.120
Well, that is, after they’d each been replaced
by an instance of SCP-3994.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:17.550
The thing no one dares to ask about humanity
looking up to the stars for so many centuries,

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:21.400
is what if someone up there was looking back
at us?

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:27.640
What if, for the entire lifetime of our civilization,
there’s been a race of alien creatures attempting

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:34.210
to study us, venturing to our backwater, small
town of a planet, and taking the form of humans

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.460
for some nefarious purpose?

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:42.330
Meet SCP-3994, that is, if you haven’t already
been acquainted with one of them.

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:47.440
They could be anyone, the local celebrity
in your small town, a person who you pass

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:51.230
on the street every day, even a wild animal.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:58.900
You see, SCP-3994 refers to a race of extraterrestrials,
beings not of our world, and a currently unknown

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:03.880
number of them have been cataloged by the
SCP Foundation.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:10.670
SCP-3994s tend to hide in plain sight, through
the use of convincing human skin disguises,

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:11.740
or ‘shells’.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:17.350
Well, while these shells might start by looking
convincing, in actual fact they’re far from

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:18.350
perfect.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:24.270
Almost seventy percent of SCP-3994 shells
experience some form of rapid degradation,

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:28.910
and this causes the imperfections in their
disguises to shine through.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:33.830
A deteriorating human shell usually results
in a number of physical deformities.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:39.770
An SCP-3994 instance wearing its shell might
appear as someone with a limb that twists

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:45.110
and bends in an unnatural way, but showing
no signs of actually noticing it.

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:49.680
Alternatively, a person who seems to have
a skeleton that doesn’t match their external

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:54.310
bodily proportions might also be an extraterrestrial
in hiding.

00:14:54.310 --> 00:15:00.320
And then, there’s the growths that some
SCP-3994 shells have.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:05.750
These are severe malformations that resemble
elephantiasis: a medical condition that causes

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.690
certain areas of the body to enlarge.

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:14.310
But just looking out for these tells isn’t
a sure-fire way of spotting one of these aliens.

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:18.930
Not all their shells have the same levels
of decay, in fact, the Foundation has developed

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:25.000
sub-categories of SCP-3994 instances based
on how noticeable their shells are.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:32.160
Category A are SCP-3994s whose shells are
almost impossible to detect, practically resembling

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.320
human beings one to one.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:38.920
On the other side, are the Category Cs, which
are members of the same extra-terrestrial

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:41.670
species without shells.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:48.339
And between them, in Category B, are the ones
whose shells are showing signs of decay.

00:15:48.339 --> 00:15:55.300
Another method the SCP Foundation has used
to detect instances of SCP-3994 is speech.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:59.800
In almost forty percent of conversations,
these aliens will attempt to mimic the speech

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:02.920
patterns of the human they are conversing
with.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:09.160
This can be as blatant as SCP-3994s echoing
back elements of speech as hard to replicate

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:14.650
as regional accents and dialects, different
languages, or specific phrases unique to the

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.120
person they’re copying.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:22.430
While in some instances SCP-3994s have shown
difficulty with grammar and syntax at first,

00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:24.550
they seem to be quick learners.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:29.210
Couple that with the almost-perfect shells
in Category A, and these alien visitors could

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.870
prove to be formidable infiltrators.

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:36.240
Researchers even discovered telepathic communications
between instances.

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:41.710
Eventually, though, all SCP-3994 shells do
inevitably decay.

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:46.080
This usually takes around a year, as their
human disguises gradually dissolve until the

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:48.420
creature beneath is eventually exposed.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:54.030
That’s where the various protrusions, misshapen
body parts, and other signs of decay come

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.030
from.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:17:00.460
It’s not that SCP-3994s are intentionally
walking around with noticeable shells, it’s

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:04.720
that they can’t prevent their shells from
eventually withering away until their true

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:07.409
self is put on display.

00:17:07.409 --> 00:17:09.600
And what do they look like under their disguises?

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:14.169
Are they tall, slender, grey-skinned beings
with long heads?

00:17:14.169 --> 00:17:18.110
Are they tiny little green men piloting human-sized
robot suits?

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:23.319
Could they even be bulbous creatures of living
calcium with huge claws, kept concealed and

00:17:23.319 --> 00:17:27.629
compressed in skin suits with zippers hidden
under their hairlines?

00:17:27.629 --> 00:17:30.289
Well, no, to all of these.

00:17:30.289 --> 00:17:33.039
That’d be terribly cliche, don’t you think?

00:17:33.039 --> 00:17:38.340
Beneath their rapidly decaying shells is a
viscous, pulp-like substance, of formless

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:41.289
and unquantifiable composition.

00:17:41.289 --> 00:17:48.700
Without their disguises, SCP-3994 have no
regular shape, no skeleton or body structure.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:54.409
Underneath, each of them is just an indeterminate
mass that drags itself around aimlessly.

00:17:54.409 --> 00:17:58.730
So, the one question that remains is… why?

00:17:58.730 --> 00:18:00.240
Why come to Earth?

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:03.000
Why replicate and replace innocent humans?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:07.220
Why spend so much time trying to learn how
to blend in as a part of our civilization

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:10.760
- like sinister imposters among us?

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:16.049
Well, the ones in Foundation captivity seem
to be pretty eager to leave.

00:18:16.049 --> 00:18:19.830
During multiple incidents, they have been
known to create shells that mimic the appearance

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:26.350
of security staff, scientists, and other Foundation
personnel in order to orchestrate their escape.

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:30.110
All the while, they’ve been showing themselves
capable of learning how to impersonate human

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:32.039
speech and mannerisms.

00:18:32.039 --> 00:18:34.580
But what is it all for?

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:36.730
The best answer is, we don’t know.

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:40.030
Or rather, we don’t know yet.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:42.370
Could they be here to study humanity?

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:47.669
Do these SCP-3994s want to learn how to be
more like us for their own benefit?

00:18:47.669 --> 00:18:53.840
Think about it, if you had no shape, no body,
if you were just a formless mass, wouldn’t

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:55.669
you feel a little…

00:18:55.669 --> 00:18:56.669
lonely?

00:18:56.669 --> 00:19:00.830
SCP-3994, like humans, might be social animals.

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:06.850
The difference is we can hug each other, high-five
each other, converse, form meaningful connections

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:08.429
through talking and touch.

00:19:08.429 --> 00:19:13.440
It could be that’s what these extra-terrestrial
imposters want, why they decided to venture

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:16.480
across the stars to live among us.

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:17.980
That’d be nice, right?

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:20.650
But then there’s the other explanation.

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:29.429
SCP-3994 are an alien army hiding out on Earth,
learning more and more about us day by day.

00:19:29.429 --> 00:19:35.660
The more they learn, the better they’ll
get at copying us, walking, talking, and acting

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:38.850
no different from any other human.

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:42.080
The Foundation doesn’t even know just how
many are out there.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:48.779
Soon, they could have perfectly mimicked every
language, every culture, every person on Earth.

00:19:48.779 --> 00:19:50.370
And what happens then?

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:52.929
What happens when we all get replaced?

00:19:52.929 --> 00:19:57.749
Well, at that point, the planet would no longer
belong to us.

00:19:57.749 --> 00:20:03.450
It would be the new home for SCP-3994.

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:10.970
Now go check out “SCP-2086 Man Eating Bus”
and “SCP-939 With Many Voices - The Complete

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:14.419
Story” for more anomalies that are hiding
in plain sight!

